    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist: Multi-Node Language-Model Serving System\n\n## Scope and Preconditions\n\nBefore running any validation, establish the test envelope:\n\n- [ ] **System topology documented**: number of nodes, GPUs/accelerators per node, interconnect (NVLink, InfiniBand, Ethernet), and the parallelism strategy in use (tensor parallel, pipeline parallel, data parallel, expert parallel, or combinations).\n- [ ] **Serving framework version pinned**: exact commit hash or release version of the inference server (e.g., vLLM, TensorRT-LLM, Triton, custom stack), plus driver, CUDA/ROCm, NCCL/Gloo versions.\n- [ ] **Model artifact identity recorded**: model hash (not just name), tokenizer hash, quantization method and calibration data reference, dtype, and any LoRA/adapters loaded.\n- [ ] **Baseline established**: a single-node or single-replica reference configuration exists so multi-node results have something to compare against.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\nGoal: prove that every node believes it is running the *same* system.\n\n- [ ] **Config hash broadcast and compared**: compute a hash over the full effective configuration (model config, parallelism settings, KV-cache size, max sequence length, sampling defaults, scheduler policy) on every node; assert all hashes match. Do not rely on \"we deployed the same YAML\" \u2014 verify the *resolved* config, after defaults, env vars, and overrides are applied.\n- [ ] **Environment parity check**: capture `nvidia-smi -q` (or equivalent), driver versions, library versions, and relevant environment variables on each node; diff them and investigate any divergence, even \"harmless\" ones.\n- [ ] **World size and rank mapping verified**: each node reports its rank, local rank, and world size; the union must equal the expected topology with no gaps or duplicates.\n- [ ] **Launch mechanism audited",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
